    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.extra\n\n### Description\n\nWhen an LSP operation like definition or implementation returns a single result, the picker opens only to immediately require a confirmation. It would be useful to skip the picker entirely and jump directly in that case.\n\nProposed behavior:\nAn opt-in flag on pickers.lsp local options that, when enabled and exactly one item is found, calls pick.default_choose directly without opening the picker. When zero or multiple results are found, behavior is unchanged.",
