        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hey, thanks for the workaround solution!\n\nIf that's alright I'd like to add to my case, and I'd also like to add that I'm happy to contribute with any of this too.\n\n- The global autocmd implementation will act on all pickers, including file pickers and the like. Whilst not the best example, it would auto jump if I opened a grep/file picker in a repo with only a single file. You get the point, not desirable for all pickers.\n- LSP jumps on single result is an established behavior: JetBrains, VS Code, and even `vim.lsp.buf.definition()` do it.\n- Workaround breaks with pickers that are async populated.\n\nI understand the purist angle, an API that opens a picker SHOULD always open a picker, straying from that would complicate the functionality, and it's reasonable to want to keep that. However, a solution could be to add a something like `MiniExtra.lsp_jump()` that has this as default behavior that can be used in tandem with `MiniExra.picker.lsp()` where the default expected behavior would be to jump with a picker fallback if more results are found.\n\nWhat do you think?",
