            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I'm not familiar with the code base so I wonder about adding this (based off the `on_list` example from `:h vim.lsp.ListOpts`) to the `on_list` function supplied by `lsp_make_opts`:\n```lua\nif #items == 1 then\n  vim.fn.setqflist({}, \" \", data)\n  vim.cmd.cfirst()\n  return\nend\n```\nThrough my monkey patching it gives that desired behavior (tested with definition only though) but I feel as if there's side effects I'm missing, or will it rather just stick to the \"calling a function to open a picker should always open a picker\" design?",
